1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,881
Clothes need two cycles to dry, and the

2
00:00:02,891 --> 00:00:04,678
laundry room feels hot?

3
00:00:05,224 --> 00:00:08,674
A clogged dryer vent wastes energy, and it

4
00:00:08,684 --> 00:00:10,552
is a real fire risk.

5
00:00:11,215 --> 00:00:14,952
Seven steps clear the lint safely, in
about an hour.

6
00:00:15,917 --> 00:00:18,682
Stay for step four: you won't believe how

7
00:00:18,692 --> 00:00:20,351
much lint comes out.

8
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:21,918
WikiTube.

9
00:00:22,279 --> 00:00:23,996
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:27,566
Every load leaves lint, and not all of

11
00:00:27,576 --> 00:00:29,061
it stops in the trap.

12
00:00:29,608 --> 00:00:33,334
The rest travels into the duct and slowly
builds up.

13
00:00:33,787 --> 00:00:38,140
Lint is highly flammable, and a blocked
vent traps heat.

14
00:00:38,594 --> 00:00:41,287
Always unplug the dryer before you start.

15
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:43,669
If you have a gas dryer, or you're

16
00:00:43,679 --> 00:00:46,244
not comfortable, call a professional.

17
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,298
You'll need a dryer vent brush kit, a

18
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:52,130
vacuum with a hose, a screwdriver for the

19
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:56,052
clamps, foil tape and gloves, and a
flashlight.

20
00:00:56,413 --> 00:00:59,024
A helper makes moving the dryer easier.

21
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:00,553
Step one.

22
00:01:01,216 --> 00:01:04,106
Turn off the dryer and unplug it from the
wall.

23
00:01:04,559 --> 00:01:06,848
If you have a gas dryer, also turn

24
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:09,716
off the gas valve, and do not disconnect

25
00:01:09,726 --> 00:01:11,373
the gas line yourself.

26
00:01:11,734 --> 00:01:13,686
If you're not sure about your type of

27
00:01:13,696 --> 00:01:15,762
dryer, call a professional.

28
00:01:16,425 --> 00:01:18,644
Let the dryer cool for at least thirty

29
00:01:18,654 --> 00:01:20,859
minutes if you recently used it.

30
00:01:21,823 --> 00:01:24,495
Clear the area around it, put on gloves

31
00:01:24,505 --> 00:01:28,265
and a dust mask, and open a window for
ventilation.

32
00:01:29,230 --> 00:01:31,426
Never skip this, since it is the most

33
00:01:31,436 --> 00:01:34,082
important safety step in the whole job.

34
00:01:34,633 --> 00:01:35,665
Step two.

35
00:01:35,956 --> 00:01:38,695
Slowly slide the dryer away from the wall,

36
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:41,121
just far enough to reach the back.

37
00:01:41,413 --> 00:01:44,386
Ask someone to help, and protect the floor

38
00:01:44,396 --> 00:01:46,381
with a towel or cardboard.

39
00:01:47,531 --> 00:01:49,750
Watch the vent hose and the power cord

40
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:50,758
as you move it.

41
00:01:51,908 --> 00:01:54,533
Don't stretch or crush them, and make sure

42
00:01:54,543 --> 00:01:57,828
that a gas dryer's flexible line does not
kink.

43
00:01:58,375 --> 00:02:00,976
If there's too little space, leave the
dryer

44
00:02:00,986 --> 00:02:04,341
where it is, and clean the duct from the
outside.

45
00:02:04,795 --> 00:02:07,420
Ask your landlord or building manager
first if

46
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:11,516
you rent, because some buildings arrange
this service for tenants.

47
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:13,065
Step three.

48
00:02:13,426 --> 00:02:15,564
Find the vent duct connecting the back of

49
00:02:15,574 --> 00:02:16,989
the dryer to the wall.

50
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:20,240
It's held by metal clamps or foil tape.

51
00:02:20,601 --> 00:02:23,412
Loosen the clamps with a screwdriver, or
peel

52
00:02:23,422 --> 00:02:25,827
off the tape, and gently pull the duct

53
00:02:25,837 --> 00:02:28,007
free from the dryer and the wall.

54
00:02:28,368 --> 00:02:29,481
Look inside.

55
00:02:29,842 --> 00:02:33,034
If it's packed with lint, you're in the
right place.

56
00:02:33,395 --> 00:02:36,795
Check the duct for holes, crushing, or
damage,

57
00:02:36,854 --> 00:02:39,225
and if it's plastic or foil, plan to

58
00:02:39,235 --> 00:02:40,778
replace it with metal.

59
00:02:41,742 --> 00:02:44,495
Tighten the clamps again after you clean,
so

60
00:02:44,505 --> 00:02:47,119
no lint escapes into the room, and the

61
00:02:47,129 --> 00:02:48,858
joint stays sealed.

62
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,351
Step four.

63
00:02:50,642 --> 00:02:53,593
Attach the brush to the flexible rod, and

64
00:02:53,603 --> 00:02:54,972
connect it to a drill.

65
00:02:55,634 --> 00:02:58,214
Feed it into the duct, running the drill

66
00:02:58,224 --> 00:03:01,442
slowly in a clockwise direction, and add
more

67
00:03:01,452 --> 00:03:02,670
rods as you go.

68
00:03:03,332 --> 00:03:06,071
Pull the brush back and forth to loosen
the lint.

69
00:03:06,618 --> 00:03:09,717
Then use the vacuum hose to remove what's
come out.

70
00:03:10,681 --> 00:03:15,675
Do this from both ends, inside and
outside,

71
00:03:15,685 --> 00:03:16,590
if you can.

72
00:03:16,881 --> 00:03:19,539
Repeat until no more lint comes out.

73
00:03:20,086 --> 00:03:22,117
Wear a dust mask throughout.

74
00:03:22,477 --> 00:03:24,708
If the duct is long, more than thirty

75
00:03:24,718 --> 00:03:27,887
feet or ten metres, or has several bends,

76
00:03:28,015 --> 00:03:30,325
consider hiring a professional.

77
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:31,923
Step five.

78
00:03:32,377 --> 00:03:35,557
Go outside, and find the vent hood on the
wall.

79
00:03:36,011 --> 00:03:38,285
Check that the flap opens freely.

80
00:03:38,577 --> 00:03:41,957
Remove any lint, leaves, bird nests or
debris

81
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:44,253
blocking it, wearing gloves.

82
00:03:44,707 --> 00:03:46,926
If you see a screen or mesh covering

83
00:03:46,936 --> 00:03:50,072
the opening, remove it, because it clogs
with

84
00:03:50,082 --> 00:03:51,939
lint and shouldn't be there.

85
00:03:53,089 --> 00:03:55,944
Clean the hood with a brush and a damp
cloth.

86
00:03:56,746 --> 00:03:59,802
Later, once the duct is reconnected,
you'll run

87
00:03:59,812 --> 00:04:03,433
the dryer and confirm that air flows out
strongly here.

88
00:04:03,887 --> 00:04:06,359
If it's weak, there is still a blockage.

89
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:09,020
Keep bushes and snow away from the outside

90
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:13,093
vent, since anything covering it will cut
airflow right away.

91
00:04:13,633 --> 00:04:14,689
Step six.

92
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:17,315
Pull out the lint screen inside the dryer

93
00:04:17,325 --> 00:04:20,331
door, and remove all lint by hand.

94
00:04:21,133 --> 00:04:23,724
Wash it with warm soapy water and a

95
00:04:23,734 --> 00:04:27,311
soft brush every few months, as fabric
softener

96
00:04:27,321 --> 00:04:29,863
leaves a film that blocks airflow.

97
00:04:30,525 --> 00:04:32,127
Let it dry completely.

98
00:04:32,488 --> 00:04:35,241
Use the vacuum's narrow attachment to
clean the

99
00:04:35,251 --> 00:04:37,830
slot where the trap sits, and the back

100
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:40,359
of the dryer where the duct connects.

101
00:04:41,021 --> 00:04:44,260
Clean the lint screen after every load as
a habit.

102
00:04:45,062 --> 00:04:47,850
Signs of a clogged vent include clothes
that

103
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:52,468
stay damp, a hot dryer top, and a burning
smell.

104
00:04:53,033 --> 00:04:54,112
Step seven.

105
00:04:54,914 --> 00:04:58,036
Reattach the duct to the dryer and the
wall.

106
00:04:58,583 --> 00:05:01,301
Use a rigid or semi-rigid metal duct if

107
00:05:01,311 --> 00:05:05,051
possible, rather than foil or plastic,
which can

108
00:05:05,061 --> 00:05:07,069
trap lint and catch fire.

109
00:05:08,033 --> 00:05:10,136
Keep the duct as short and straight as

110
00:05:10,146 --> 00:05:13,085
you can, and secure the joints with clamps

111
00:05:13,095 --> 00:05:16,925
or foil tape, not screws, which catch
lint.

112
00:05:17,890 --> 00:05:20,850
Push the dryer back without crushing the
duct,

113
00:05:20,979 --> 00:05:24,205
plug it in, and run it for a few minutes.

114
00:05:24,752 --> 00:05:27,177
Check outside for strong airflow.

115
00:05:27,538 --> 00:05:29,293
Make a note on your calendar for next

116
00:05:29,303 --> 00:05:32,518
year, and keep the brush kit somewhere
handy.

117
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:35,368
If the dryer is still slow, look for

118
00:05:35,378 --> 00:05:36,584
the next cause.

119
00:05:36,945 --> 00:05:39,918
Check the outside flap, and make sure it

120
00:05:39,928 --> 00:05:42,214
opens fully when the dryer runs.

121
00:05:43,179 --> 00:05:45,558
Pour a little water on the lint screen.

122
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:48,707
If it pools instead of soaking in, a

123
00:05:48,717 --> 00:05:52,594
film of softener is blocking the mesh, so
scrub it.

124
00:05:53,396 --> 00:05:55,952
Look for sharp bends or a crushed duct

125
00:05:55,962 --> 00:05:57,331
behind the dryer.

126
00:05:57,784 --> 00:06:00,654
Do not overload the drum, because clothes
need

127
00:06:00,664 --> 00:06:01,917
room to tumble.

128
00:06:02,467 --> 00:06:05,368
Some vents are not a do-it-yourself job.

129
00:06:05,822 --> 00:06:08,169
If the duct runs a long way, through

130
00:06:08,179 --> 00:06:11,440
the roof, or inside a wall or ceiling,

131
00:06:11,615 --> 00:06:13,994
a professional has the right tools.

132
00:06:14,285 --> 00:06:17,163
The same goes for any gas dryer problem.

133
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:20,068
If you smell gas, leave the house and

134
00:06:20,078 --> 00:06:21,459
call the gas company.

135
00:06:21,913 --> 00:06:25,281
If a burning smell returns after cleaning,
unplug

136
00:06:25,291 --> 00:06:27,972
the dryer and have a technician check it.

137
00:06:28,533 --> 00:06:30,831
Small habits do most of the work.

138
00:06:31,377 --> 00:06:34,514
Empty the lint screen after every load,
because

139
00:06:34,524 --> 00:06:36,938
it is the first place lint collects.

140
00:06:38,088 --> 00:06:39,982
Do not run the dryer when you are

141
00:06:39,992 --> 00:06:41,814
out of the house or asleep.

142
00:06:42,105 --> 00:06:45,842
Never dry items that contain gasoline,
cooking oil

143
00:06:46,018 --> 00:06:49,305
or other flammable substances, because
they can heat

144
00:06:49,315 --> 00:06:50,475
up on their own.

145
00:06:51,021 --> 00:06:53,426
Keep the area around the dryer clear of

146
00:06:53,436 --> 00:06:57,058
clutter, and keep a working smoke alarm
nearby.

147
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,747
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

148
00:07:00,549 --> 00:07:03,706
First, working on a plugged-in or gas
dryer

149
00:07:03,730 --> 00:07:05,622
without the right precautions.

150
00:07:06,075 --> 00:07:09,789
Always unplug, and call a pro for gas.

151
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:14,587
Second, using a foil or plastic duct, or

152
00:07:14,597 --> 00:07:18,543
long, bendy runs, which collect lint and
hold heat.

153
00:07:18,904 --> 00:07:21,469
And third, waiting too long.

154
00:07:22,271 --> 00:07:24,511
Clean the vent at least once a year,

155
00:07:24,535 --> 00:07:27,658
or sooner if drying takes longer than
usual.

156
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:30,899
If you notice a burning smell, stop using

157
00:07:30,909 --> 00:07:33,381
the dryer and investigate straight away.

158
00:07:33,742 --> 00:07:36,356
Treat any burning smell as a warning, and

159
00:07:36,366 --> 00:07:37,596
don't ignore it.

160
00:07:38,133 --> 00:07:39,247
Let's recap.

161
00:07:40,397 --> 00:07:41,790
Unplug the dryer.

162
00:07:42,023 --> 00:07:43,427
Pull it out carefully.

163
00:07:44,577 --> 00:07:46,132
Disconnect the duct.

164
00:07:47,282 --> 00:07:49,870
Clean the duct with a brush and a vacuum.

165
00:07:50,162 --> 00:07:52,169
Clean the outside vent hood.

166
00:07:52,832 --> 00:07:55,037
Clean the lint trap and housing.

167
00:07:55,398 --> 00:07:59,263
And reconnect with a metal duct, then test
the airflow.

168
00:07:59,926 --> 00:08:03,399
Seven steps, about an hour, and a dryer

169
00:08:03,409 --> 00:08:05,741
that dries faster and safer.

170
00:08:06,892 --> 00:08:09,644
Bonus sections cover what to check if
drying

171
00:08:09,654 --> 00:08:12,440
is still slow, when to call a
professional,

172
00:08:12,499 --> 00:08:15,760
and the daily habits that prevent dryer
fires.

173
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:18,401
That's how you clean your dryer vent.

174
00:08:18,854 --> 00:08:20,818
If this saved you energy and gave you

175
00:08:20,828 --> 00:08:24,475
peace of mind, subscribe to WikiTube,
because we

176
00:08:24,485 --> 00:08:27,433
publish a new how-to every single day.

177
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,827
Tell us in the comments how much lint

178
00:08:29,837 --> 00:08:31,836
you found, and what you would like us

179
00:08:31,846 --> 00:08:33,203
to explain next.

180
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:34,840
See you tomorrow.

181
00:08:35,131 --> 00:08:37,896
And clean your lint trap after every load,

182
00:08:37,906 --> 00:08:39,020
as a habit.

183
00:08:39,133 --> 00:08:40,351
That's WikiTube.

184
00:08:40,642 --> 00:08:42,812
Whatever it is, here's how.
